  {"_type":"illness_script","topic":"Endocrine Emergencies in the ICU","discipline":"anesthesia","enabling_conditions":"Thyroid storm: iodine load, surgery/illness in untreated hyperthyroid; DI: brain death, pituitary surgery, head trauma; Adrenal crisis: steroid withdrawal, bilateral adrenal hemorrhage, critical illness","pathophysiology":"Thyroid storm: uncontrolled T3/T4 excess driving hypermetabolism; DI: absent ADH causing free water loss; adrenal crisis: absent cortisol impairing vasopressor responsiveness and glucose regulation","time_course":"Thyroid storm: acute over hours with precipitant; DI: within hours of pituitary injury; adrenal crisis: insidious then acute decompensation","key_features":"Thyroid storm: hyperthermia, tachycardia, altered mental status, AF; DI: massive dilute polyuria, hypernatremia; adrenal crisis: refractory hypotension, hyponatremia, hypoglycemia","consequence_if_missed":"Thyroid storm: cardiovascular collapse, multi-organ failure; DI: severe hypernatremia, organ damage in donor; adrenal crisis: vasopressor-refractory shock, death"}
